almost two years ago i posted a video on  the six reasons why i quit social media  and with the exception of youtube it's  hard to believe that it will soon be  almost seven years that i decided to  delete my facebook account and go  without any accounts such as twitter  instagram tock to quit social media for  good in my previous video i shared about  my addiction to social media and how i  lived for the likes and posting that  perfect photo instead of living in the  present moment the fomo that i  experienced and the negative side  effects that it had on me such as  insecurity comparison and just an  overall feeling of anxiety and  inadequacy and so today i want to share  with you how my decision to quit social  media has changed my life dramatically  as a millennial soon graduating from  college everyone i knew had social media  all of my classmates were on facebook  and had facebook groups even my teachers  and instagram was just starting to blow  up i've gotten some comments saying that  quitting social media is trendy and that  may be the case now and i'm glad that  there's an awareness about this issue  but it was definitely not the trend at  the time i was definitely regarded as  the weirdo the odd one out and that some  of my classmates thought was just a  loser who probably didn't have any  friends or a social life that was worth  posting about and in the beginning  especially my classmate's perceptions of  me was of huge importance to me and it  began to instill doubt in me maybe i was  the loner loser with no social life  maybe my life was too boring too  pointless to post about  maybe they were right  at that stage of my life i had not  realized that i was going through  withdrawal for years i had allowed  myself to be programmed to instantly  reach for my phone and snap a photo of  something and post it the moment  something interesting happened or to  check my notifications the moment i had  just even one or two minutes of idle  time i had lost the ability to be still  be quiet and be present  and as dr cal newport puts it i had lost  my intellectual independence and the  worst part is i gave it up willingly to  a device that took up hours of my day  for something that only left me feeling  empty i've been told that it's pointless  to leave social media if you're going to  swap it out for the next bad habit like  binge watching netflix day in and day  out and i was actually very aware of  that i had reached a point in my life  when i felt so empty i questioned what i  was doing with my life and what the  point of it all was  i made my decision to quit social media  because  i was tired of living a superficial life  i was tired of pretending to be this  happy carefree 20-something-year-old  when in reality i struggled with social  anxiety to the degree that i would start  sweating my heart would start racing if  i even had to call someone over the  phone instead of via text and that i  struggled daily with self-loathing and  self-doubt and i decided that if i was  going to quit social media cold turkey  that to make it easier for myself i was  going to replace it with things that  would make me happier and that is where  the first major change comes in  i have a question for you on a scale of  0 to 10 how would you rate your social  interactions this can be something you  just think of in your own mind or you  can post it in the comments and we can  chat about it together but do think  about it i have a video where i talk  more about my journey with social  anxiety and what i specifically did to  beat the struggle that i had it was  around this time that i realized that i  had to change and i came across vanessa  van edwards and i started to apply a lot  of the lessons that she teaches i began  to force myself to go out because it  made me anxious i forced myself to lead  events initiate conversations and even  make eye contact with the person in the  elevator and smile and something amazing  happened i began to have more meaningful  and deeper conversations with my friends  and family and even perfect strangers  and i began to crave that and want more  of those deeper conversations and my  focus completely shifted from what will  people think of me to  how can i make this person feel valuable  how can i make them feel that they  matter and when my mindset shifted from  worrying about whether or not people  would like me to focus on liking other  people i now had the ability to love  other people and genuinely see them the  way that i had wanted to be seen and it  felt like freedom  [Music]  i have another question for you who are  you investing in i know that when i had  social media i spent hours upon hours  following the lives of my friends and  celebrities admiring their lives and  wishing that mine could be more  glamorous when i left those sites i  found myself with time i had time to sit  quietly with myself and ask who am i  what do i want from my life what do i  want to leave behind when i die i  realized that i had been so focused on  keeping up with the kardashians and  investing my time in them and in other  people that i wasn't investing in myself  and so i took this time and i began to  go out in nature more go on hikes and  exercise and i also started to eat  better i started to listen to audiobooks  on my commutes and i changed the way  that i consumed content i stopped  watching tv and then later on we  actually ended up getting rid of our tv  all together i did mention that youtube  is the account that i did decide to keep  and i found myself with a much greater  awareness of the value of my time i  could no longer just sit through  watching funny videos vlogs or just  videos that were meant to entertain i  instead began to use it to search for  content that would help me learn  something new or improve my life in some  way and as all of these sorts of things  slowly started changing little by little  i found myself perceiving myself  differently i was more forgiving of  myself i was more open to trying new  things to experimenting and making  mistakes and i found myself with a spark  of creativity and this is where  everything changed for me  do you want to be a consumer or a  producer when i began to place greater  value in my social interactions and  value other people i began to have a  greater value for myself i began to see  that i had something that was worth  sharing and it was this change in me  that gave me permission to be creative i  was in a live play with an audience of  over 1500 people and i began to explore  the idea that maybe i wasn't meant to  sit and watch the play  maybe i was meant to be in the play and  this metaphorical play is life i no  longer wanted life to happen to me i  wanted to live my life with intention  by now many of us know that social media  is designed to be addictive after all  the very people who design casinos work  diligently to make sure that you stay  glued to your device as long as possible  but i also don't think that social media  is evil i have no doubt that social  media can be helpful and many  individuals make a living off of social  media others buy or sell through it or  even have support groups that otherwise  wouldn't be available to them in person  but when it comes to the way you use  social media it can go either two ways  either you're using it or it's using you  and that decision is yours alone to make  do you want to sit and watch the play or  do you want to be in the play you get to  decide  i thank you so much for watching if you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up and subscribe so that you won't miss  when i post a new video i can't wait to  hear from you in the comments and see  you in the next video bye for now  [Music]  you
 

